{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_http_endpoints", "label": "Management HTTP endpoints (page)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_health_endpoint", "label": "GET /health", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Liveness; 503 with status DOWN if any liveness check fails."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_ready_endpoint", "label": "GET /ready", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "clusterReady is cluster-membership own result read back out of the checks array rather than computed separately, so it is false until the local node reaches Up and true when there is no cluster at all."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_cluster_members_endpoint", "label": "GET /cluster/members", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_cluster_leader_endpoint", "label": "GET /cluster/leader", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "leader is null before one is elected; useful for monitoring leadership churn."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_cluster_shards_endpoint", "label": "GET /cluster/shards", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Answered from the last map the coordinator broadcast to this node region, so nothing needs configuring \u2014 it used to read the coordinator DistributedData snapshot, which made a 200 unreachable in a default configuration. A node that never mentioned the type answers 404, and a 200 with an empty shardHome is normal."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_metrics_endpoint", "label": "GET /metrics (opt-in)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_cluster_leave_endpoint", "label": "POST /cluster/leave (opt-in)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One-way: once a node leaves it cannot rejoin in the same process because its membership state is gone. Anyone with port access can drain your node, so gate it behind authentication."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_cluster_down_endpoint", "label": "POST /cluster/down (opt-in)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Destructive and irrecoverable \u2014 the target actors stop and its shards reallocate, and the downed node sees MemberRemoved for itself. High-risk: gate behind auth plus audit logs."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_policy_split", "label": "auth and ipAllowlist policy split", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "auth wraps the privileged subset while /health and /ready stay anonymous, because Kubernetes probes cannot easily attach an Authorization header; ipAllowlist wraps every endpoint including them, because network-level isolation is independent of who is authenticated."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_bearertokenauth", "label": "BearerTokenAuth", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shared-secret bearer token with rotation via multiple entries; a missing or wrong header answers 401 with WWW-Authenticate."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_ipallowlist", "label": "IpAllowlist on the management tree", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A client IP outside the allowlist, or unresolvable, answers 403."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_topology_disclosure", "label": "Read-only endpoints still reveal topology", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Member addresses, roles, the leader and the shard map are internal state, so the management server is sensitive even where nothing is writable \u2014 bind it internally and gate it."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_http_endpoints", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_health_endpoint", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_http_endpoints", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_ready_endpoint", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_http_endpoints", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_cluster_members_endpoint", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_http_endpoints", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_cluster_leader_endpoint", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/http-endpoints.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_http_endpoints", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_http_endpoints_cluster_shards_endpoint", "